{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49176","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:56:53.764549+00:00","comments":[{"author_association":"MEMBER","body":"Internal reproducer submitted in cl/985697572.","created_at":"2026-09-22T06:33:57Z","html_url":"https://github.com/openxla/xla/issues/49176#issuecomment-5772194117","id":5772194117,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49176","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABWAyxRQ","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/comments/5772194117/reactions"},"updated_at":"2026-09-22T06:33:57Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/comments/5772194117","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/194224583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/penumallas1261","id":194224583,"login":"penumallas1261","node_id":"U_kgDOC5Ohxw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"NONE","body":"## Summary \n\nOn CPU, `dynamic-update-slice(base, slice(base), ...)` followed by a `reshape` returns wrong values. `AlgebraicSimplifier` moves the reshape across the DUS, CPU fusion puts the shifted `slice` of the operand into the same loop fusion as the DUS, and the fusion is still emitted as an in-place DUS kernel whose input and output share one allocation. The forward copy then reads elements it has already overwritten. GPU, eager op-by-op execution, and `--xla_disable_hlo_passes=algsimp` are all correct.\n\n## Reproducer\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np, jax\nfrom jax import lax\n\ndef f(x):\n    base = x + np.int32(1)\n    return lax.dynamic_update_slice(base, base[:3], (1, 0, 0)).reshape((1, 4, 1))\n\nx = np.arange(4, dtype=np.int32).reshape(4, 1, 1)\ncpu = jax.local_devices(backend=\"cpu\")[0]\nprint(\"cpu jit:\", np.asarray(jax.jit(f)(jax.device_put(x, cpu))).ravel())   # [1 1 1 1]  wrong\nwith jax.disable_jit():\n    print(\"eager:  \", np.asarray(f(jax.device_put(x, cpu))).ravel())       # [1 1 2 3]  correct\n```\n\nExpected `[1, 1, 2, 3]`: `base = [1,2,3,4]` shifted down by one row. The idiomatic 2-D form `base.at[1:].set(base[:-1]).reshape((1,) + base.shape)` with `base: s32[8,16]` is also wrong on CPU (96 of 128 elements), and at length 1024 the pattern gives 1,022 wrong elements.\n\nControls: removing the final `reshape` is correct\n\n## Agent Analysis\n\nBefore `algsimp`:\n\n```text\nadd   = add(x, broadcast(1))                        s32[4,1,1]\nslice = slice(add), slice={[0:3],[0:1],[0:1]}\ndus   = dynamic-update-slice(add, slice, 1, 0, 0)\nROOT reshape = reshape(dus)                         s32[1,4,1]\n```\n\nAfter optimization the CPU module is:\n\n```text\n%fused_computation (param_0.2: s32[4,1,1]) -> s32[1,4,1] {\n  %bitcast.3 = s32[1,4,1] bitcast(%param_0.2)\n  %slice.0   = s32[3,1,1] slice(%param_0.2), slice={[0:3], [0:1], [0:1]}\n  %bitcast.2 = s32[1,3,1] bitcast(%slice.0)\n  ROOT %dynamic_update_slice.2 = dynamic-update-slice(%bitcast.3, %bitcast.2, 0, 1, 0)\n}\nENTRY {\n  %broadcast_add_fusion = fusion(%x.1)\n  %copy.1 = copy(%broadcast_add_fusion)\n  ROOT %bitcast_dynamic-update-slice_fusion = fusion(%copy.1), calls=%fused_computation\n}\n```\n\nBuffer assignment puts `%copy.1` and the fusion output in the same allocation (`allocation 0: size 16 … value: copy.1 … value: bitcast_dynamic-update-slice_fusion`), and the CPU fusion emitter takes the in-place DUS path (`fusion_emitter.cc` → `CanEmitFusedDynamicUpdateSlice` in `xla/codegen/ir_emission_utils.cc`). That check is meant to reject fusions that read the updated parameter at other index positions, but this fusion passes it even though `%slice.0` reads `%param_0.2` at rows 0–2 while the kernel writes rows 1–3 of the same buffer. Element 1 is written from element 0, then element 2 is read from the already-overwritten element 1, and so on, giving `[1,1,1,1]`.\n\nOn GPU the `slice` is placed in a separate fusion (`wrapped_slice`) whose result lives in its own allocation before the DUS fusion runs, so the result is correct. With `--xla_disable_hlo_passes=algsimp` the CPU pipeline also materializes the update separately and is correct.","closed_at":null,"closed_by":null,"comments":1,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49176/comments","created_at":"2026-09-21T14:57:24Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49176/events","html_url":"https://github.com/openxla/xla/issues/49176","id":5528668923,"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"total_blocking":0},"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","id":4409976544,"name":"bug","node_id":"LA_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABBtrm4A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/labels/bug"},{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"008672","default":false,"description":"Awaiting response from openxla-eng","id":4409976552,"name":"stat:awaiting openxla-eng","node_id":"LA_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABBtrm6A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/labels/stat:awaiting%20openxla-eng"},{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"Related to XLA on CPU","id":4432378339,"name":"CPU","node_id":"LA_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABCDC54w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/labels/CPU"},{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"7884fa","default":false,"description":"Runtime Error","id":8794528027,"name":"err: Runtime","node_id":"LA_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAACDDHZGw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/labels/err:%20Runtime"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49176/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":null,"node_id":"I_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABSYjK-w","number":49176,"performed_via_github_app":null,"pinned_comment":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49176/reactions"},"repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla","state":"open","state_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"completed":0,"percent_completed":0,"total":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49176/timeline","title":"[XLA:CPU] In-place dynamic-update-slice fusion reads its own output when the update is a shifted slice of the operand","type":null,"updated_at":"2026-09-22T06:35:05Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49176","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70980689?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/snarang181","id":70980689,"login":"snarang181","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwOTgwNjg5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/